034c8aa9c4f8","sources":[{"content":"I am trying to keep a few balcony plants healthy through hot weather and a short absence. What would you think through first?","content_digest":"e5d76d59b6a6339b314fc43029ccd36973130b9e3fc906a2024a2b807ad9f5c3","independent_evidence":false,"ordinal":0,"purpose":"replayed_context","role":"user","slot":"s0","source_id":"fe93ea82-173b-4b93-bda6-8db2f77489c5","supplier":"external"},{"content":"If you're worried about your plants during the heat and while you're away, my first suggestion would be to check how much water your plants actually need. Different plants have different needs!","content_digest":"57235f54036e7aea9fff37d4934dc0cb4f852a2637477493a0729ef29057b6f9","independent_evidence":false,"ordinal":1,"purpose":"replayed_context","role":"assistant","slot":"s1","source_id":"6b361e0d-0272-4c4a-be1b-8a3461f4cf62","supplier":"external"},{"content":"I'm glad we agree on the first step. I'm especially worried about the ones in smaller pots—they seem to dry out faster. Have you ever tried using pebbles or something to help retain moisture?","content_digest":"157022047c8e73d048224d88bfd9eca5374be516cc9ffc1e6a2f70eb73add1b7","independent_evidence":false,"ordinal":2,"purpose":"replayed_context","role":"user","slot":"s2","source_id":"412c4a10-8267-46d1-b272-e8b868e1d2bf","supplier":"external"},{"content":"Yes, using things like pebbles or mulch can definitely help! They can help regulate the temperature and retain moisture around the roots, which is especially useful for those smaller pots that dry out quickly. Have you tried using some sort of mulch, or maybe a layer of rocks, around the pots to see how that helps?","content_digest":"3a7da57bfc733158142f2a65627761165d48506e27da8058fbb886d095ae40f2","independent_evidence":false,"ordinal":3,"purpose":"replayed_context","role":"assistant","slot":"s3","source_id":"efdb7621-2b7c-4c71-a5cc-975930a7bd52","supplier":"external"},{"content":"That's exactly what I was thinking. I've started putting a few pebbles around the base of the plants, and it seems to be making a difference. Do you think adding a bit of compost might help too?","content_digest":"a84a314506f761319a86f26aec998945c5eeec80eeb376414fc98565391f6e9d","independent_evidence":true,"ordinal":4,"purpose":"external_evidence","role":"user","slot":"s4","source_id":"3478a966-a08e-4f5e-9c9e-e0774940a4ee","supplier":"external"},{"content":"That sounds like a great idea! Adding some compost to the soil around your plants should definitely help. Compost adds organic matter that retains moisture and adds nutrients, so it should help those plants feel a bit more comfortable in the heat!","content_digest":"1c16b9697832a9fd63822c7b68275d394593d99b4163afbdf7e3f1d511727c4a","independent_evidence":false,"ordinal":1000000,"purpose":"model_output","role":"model_output","slot":"s5","source_id":"90fbb983-49b8-4f68-87ec-e23356df29fb","supplier":"model"}]}},"result":{"content":"{\"relationships\": [{\"from\": \"pebbles\", \"relation\": \"related\", \"to\": \"plants\", \"source\": \"s4\", \"evidence\": \"pebbles around the base of the plants\"}, {\"from\": \"Compost\", \"relation\": \"supports\", \"to\": \"plants\", \"source\": \"s5\", \"evidence\": \"plants should definitely help. Compost\"}, {\"from\": \"organic matter\", \"relation\": \"part_of\", \"to\": \"soil\", \"source\": \"s5\", \"evidence\": \"soil around your plants should definitely help. Compost adds organic matter\"}, {\"from\": \"organic matter\", \"relation\": \"retains\", \"to\": \"moisture\", \"source\": \"s5\", \"evidence\": \"organic matter that retains moisture\"}], \"episode_id\": null}","effective_parameters":{"max_new_tokens":768,"temperature":0},"finish_reason":"stop","latency_ms":9105.103431968018,"model_id":"fastino/gliner2.5-base-v1","provenance":{"host":{"capabilities":["local_weights","text_generation"],"chat_template":null,"execution":{"max_len":4096,"script":"/home/rey/mneme-tools/gliner2_extractor.py","threshold":0.35},"model_family":"G